      "Event": {
        "Id": "0",
        "DescriptionIssue": "<p style=\"margin-left:48px; margin-right:33px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">A water contact closure has been issued for San Diego River Dog Beach in Ocean Beach following a sewage release. Approximately 160,000 gallons of sewage were discharged and reached the San Diego River near the intersection of Mission Gorge Road and Junipero Serra Trail.</span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; margin-right:33px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Beachgoers are advised that the ocean water contains sewage and may cause illness. The water contact closure will remain in place until sampling and field observations confirm these areas are safe for water contact.</span></span></span></span></p>\n",
